---
type: agent/instruction
description: Create a linked worktree and hand it to a fresh agent session
usage: "guide://_worktree/new[/<branch-name>]"
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
includes:
  - ../_partials/handoff-context-target
elicitation:
  branch-name:
    message: "Choose the branch for the new worktree. An existing branch will be checked out; a new branch will be created from main."
    fallback: render
    schema:
      type: object
      properties:
        branch:
          type: string
          pattern: '^(?!-)(?!.*\.\.)(?!.*//)(?!.*(?:^|/)\.)(?!.*[/.]$)(?!.*\.lock$)[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+$'
      required: [branch]
---
{{h1}}Create linked worktree

Guide allocated the worktree name `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.

1. Create the linked worktree at `{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.
   {{#args.0.value}}Use branch `{{args.0.value}}`.{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}Use branch `{{kwargs.branch}}`.{{/args.0.value}}
   If that branch already exists, check it out. Otherwise create it from `main`,
   never from the current branch:
   ```sh
   git worktree add {{#shell_quote}}{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}{{/shell_quote}} -b {{#shell_quote}}{{#args.0.value}}{{args.0.value}}{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}{{kwargs.branch}}{{/args.0.value}}{{/shell_quote}} main
   ```
   For an existing branch, use `git worktree add {{#shell_quote}}{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}{{/shell_quote}} {{#shell_quote}}{{#args.0.value}}{{args.0.value}}{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}{{kwargs.branch}}{{/args.0.value}}{{/shell_quote}}` instead.
2. Update the shared handoff context at {{>handoff-context-target}} using the locking protocol in `_system/_handoff-context`. Add or merge only this `worktrees` entry, preserving every other top-level key:
   ```json
   {
     "worktrees": {
       "{{kwargs.worktree_name}}": {
         "path": "{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}",
         "branch": "{{#args.0.value}}{{args.0.value}}{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}{{kwargs.branch}}{{/args.0.value}}",
         "phase": "implementation",
         "instructions": "Continue the assigned implementation in this linked worktree."
       }
     }
   }
   ```
   Add `plan`, `issue`, task metadata, and more specific instructions when they
   are known.
3. Spawn the child with the allocated name `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}` and path
   `{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`. Do not forward this session ID.
   The child must report its working directory, create a fresh Guide interaction,
   bind `path: {{project.root}}` and `worktree: {{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`,
   then read its own handoff entry before continuing.
